ARUSIQ Smart AC Intelligence Platform, **Phase 1A**: a clickable prototype of
three role dashboards on **labelled simulated data**. React 19 + TS + Vite.
EN + ID. Two-week sprint.

Full context lives in `CLAUDE.md` and `context/`. Read the context file your
task needs — `context/00-INDEX.md` is the map. Do not read them all.

**The gate:** `npm run verify` (contrast · tokens · provenance · i18n · types ·
lint · trace). Run it before claiming work is done. If a check is wrong, fix the
check in `tools/` — do not add an exemption to route around it.

**Non-negotiable invariants** (full list + sources in
`context/requirements/requirements.json`):

1. Every figure carries provenance — Simulated | Estimated | Provisional |
   Verified, beside the figure. Aggregates inherit the **weakest** input.
2. Severity is colour **+ shape + label**. Never a bare dot, including in charts.
   Roll-up: `critical > warning > unknown > normal`.
3. Grey means "we do not know" — never counted as green, always with a last-seen
   time.
4. Never fabricate a value. Missing is not zero.
5. Indoor CO₂ **ppm** and **kgCO₂e** emissions never share a card, axis or icon.
6. The word "credit" is Verified-only. Phase 1A says *avoided emissions*.
7. Restriction is a four-step ladder with notice, grace and dual approval —
   never a switch. `stop` is blocked for health-sensitive spaces.
8. A command shows Sent → Acknowledged → Verified. Only Verified settles it.
9. No hardcoded user-facing strings. Locale formatting, never concatenation.
10. No screen is a dead end. Mark every mock as a mock. Light mode only.

Out of scope: real devices, notifications, payments, backend, carbon credits,
HVAC, dark mode.
